    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking at a 2022 Ford F-150 that's slipping under load. I'm running a diagnostic scan and I'm seeing some really irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. What are the most likely culprits for these kind of fluctuations in an automatic transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those irregular pressure spikes in a hydraulic circuit usually point to issues within the transmission control system or the valve body. Common culprits include a failing solenoid that is not maintaining a steady pressure, or a clogged or worn filter causing inconsistent fluid flow. It's also possible that the transmission fluid itself is old or contaminated, which can significantly affect hydraulic performance.",
