    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'll drop the valve body and take a look. One thing though—it's almost like the pressure just jumps for no reason, totally inconsistent with the gear shifts. It feels like there's something just randomly messing with the flow or causing these weird little hiccups in the system. Any idea why it would be so unpredictable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the pressure spikes are completely random and not tied to any specific shift event, it strongly suggests an unmetered or erratic vacuum/pressure input influencing the hydraulic control. Sometimes a very small, intermittent leak elsewhere in the pressurized lines, perhaps near a seal, can mimic this erratic behavior. Another possibility is a slight issue with the transmission cooler lines introducing inconsistent fluid temperature, which can affect fluid viscosity and pressure readings.",
      "source": "target",
